{
  $description: "The profiler's records and sections as the core lays them out and the client reads\nthem from the replies that hand them over (perf/record.rs, ts/client/src/service/core/perf.ts):\nword offsets, eight bytes a word. The names the numbers index are their owners':\na task's io's (spec/client/core/sys/io/demand.json5), a step's, an effect's and a part of the stage's the\nframe's (spec/client/core/perf/step.json5), a GPU span's the renderer's\n(spec/client/render/gpu/span.json5), a base layer's the bake's\n(spec/spec/bake/publication.json5). A packed table gives each field's\nwidth and the generator lays the offsets out. Nothing is built\nfor a read: the core writes numbers where they stay, and the words for them are\nthe UI's. LIMIT holds the bounds the profiler keeps, which the core and the client both read.",
  $extensions: {
    xpute: {
      uses: [
        "spec/client/core/sys/sched/phase.json5",
        "spec/client/core/sys/io/demand.json5",
        "spec/client/core/perf/step.json5",
        "spec/client/render/gpu/span.json5",
        "spec/spec/bake/publication.json5",
      ],
    },
  },
  HIT_KIND: {
    $type: "enum",
    $value: ["ground", "object", "objects", "decor"],
    $description: "What the pick met (NOW.view `hit_kind`; pxl-core domain/query/ray.rs `HitKind`): the ground, a placed cube, placed cubes folded into a coarser box, or a decor.",
    $extensions: { xpute: { names: true } },
  },
  LIMIT: {
    $type: "u32",
    REASON_CAP: { $value: 4 },
    REASON_WORDS: {
      $value: 3,
      $description: "A reason's words: its fail, its detail and how many (STREAM_STAT.reasons).",
    },
    WINDOW_MS: {
      $value: 60000,
      $description: "How far back the tables keep, the core's frames and tasks and the UI's long frames alike: the last minute.",
    },
    PAGE_SZ: {
      $value: 8192,
      $description: "The most bytes one read hands over. A table is read a page at a time (perf.wit `table`), each read from the sequence the last ended at, up to the table's end; the worst frames, the string table and the statistics each fit one page.",
    },
  },
  FRAME: {
    $description: "One frame and the interval it opened (perf/frame.rs FrameSample): every figure of one frame, landed when the next frame closes the interval. `interval_ms` is that interval, `refresh_ms` the display's interval as the frame's pacing takes it, its measured one (pxl-core sys/sched/display.rs) or one interval at RATE_MAX_HZ before it is measured (pxl-core domain/scene/rate.rs `display_ms`), and `paced_ms` the frame's target interval, which it was paced at (rate.rs `target_ms`). `settled` is 1 where the frame asked for no next one, else 0. `budget_ms` is the frame's entry's budget, the time from the entry's start to its end (pxl-core sys/sched.rs `budget_ms`): the end is the frame's target interval less MARGIN_SHARE from the frame's start, the budget is 0 where the entry started past it, and one slice from the entry's start where it started the margin past the target or later (sys/sched.rs `Budget`); and `overran` is 1 where the scheduler found the budget spent as the tick ended, the clock at or past the entry's end (sys/sched.rs `spent`), else 0. The effects, the tick, the requests' pump and the stage are the frame's parts, in that order: `effects` is each effect's time in the frame, in EFFECT_NAME's order, `tick_ms` the tick's and `phases` each of its phases', `pump_ms` the requests declared and pumped (pxl-core frame.rs `run`), and `stage_parts` each part of the stage's, in STAGE_PART_NAME's order; the effects' time and the stage's are their sums. The pump and the stage's parts are timed while the profiler records, as the effects are. `fill_ms` is what the ground's fill took in the entry after the frame's, up to that entry's budget, and `fill_brick_cnt` the bricks it filled there (pxl-core domain/layer/terrain/clipmap.rs `fill_bricks`), each 0 where no brick was due. `perf_ms` is what the profiler cost the frame, its own record of it and the UI's reads of it. `invalidations` is how many times a frame was asked for between this frame's record and the one before, by reason, in INVALIDATION_REASON's order (pxl-core sys/sched.rs `take_invalidations`): what woke the frame, what was asked while it ran, and a refused frame's ask before it; an ask for a time counts when the time comes. `gpu_timed` is 1 where the GPU's read of this frame has landed, which comes a frame or two later and is written back into this frame's record (`gpu_frame` the renderer's number of it, counted from 1, by which a frame is found in every table, 0 where it drew none): its `gpu_spans` are then that read's, `gpu_busy_ms` the time they ran, those that overlap counted once, the frame's GPU time, which the spans' sum overstates where passes overlap (pxl-render gpu/api.rs `Gpu::gpu_busy_ms`), and `gpu_px` the world's pixels of the frame the read timed, what the spans were measured over; and 0 where nothing measured it (its read not landed yet or cut off by a stop, or the device keeps no timestamps), its spans, busy time and pixels 0 too. `scale` is the share of the display's pixels, each way, the world was drawn at, in every frame (pxl-core domain/scene/resolution.rs `drawn_scale`). `kind_name` indexes the renderer's FRAME_KIND. `draw_cnt` and `triangle_cnt` are the frame's, every pipeline a draw names (pxl-render gpu/draw.rs `DRAW_PIPELINES`), counted while the profiler records. `light_changed` says what changed that cast the light's map in the frame, a bit each in LIGHT_CHANGED's order (pxl-render ray/cast.rs `light_changed`), 0 where it did not cast. The ray lanes are the `ray_cnt` setting's, written into the frame they were counted in as the counts land a frame or two later, by the renderer's number of it as a GPU read is (pxl-render ray/count.rs `RayCount`), 0 where none landed: `eye_cast` and `light_cast` 1 where the eye cast in full or the light's map cast and its counts landed; then the eye's pixels (`eye_ray_cnt`) and the light's map's slots (`light_ray_cnt`), and a cast's each: the nodes its beam rays, its samples and its holes' walk visited (`_beam`, `_sample`, `_hole_walk`), the asks of the world among the last (`_ask_cnt`), its pixels or slots that took the visible voxel, a walk of their own as holes and the sky (`_voxel`, `_hole`, `_sky`), together every one it cast again, so the light's three over `light_ray_cnt` are the share of its map a cast cast again, and the boxes drawn (pxl-engine `count`). `loads` is how many tiles each base layer's tile cache took in during the frame, in BASE_KIND's order (pxl-core domain/layer/tile_cache.rs `take_load_cnt`). `upload_cnt` and `upload_bytes` are the renderer's upload table (pxl-render renderer.rs `FrameStat`), and `heap_used_bytes` the heap's high-water mark (pxl-core sys/heap.rs `HeapStat`). A lane's name says its unit: `_ms`, `_bytes`, `_px`, and `_name` for an index into a list of names.",
    $extensions: { xpute: { packed: true } },
    t: { $value: 1 },
    interval_ms: { $value: 1 },
    refresh_ms: { $value: 1 },
    paced_ms: { $value: 1 },
    settled: { $value: 1 },
    budget_ms: { $value: 1 },
    overran: { $value: 1 },
    tick_ms: { $value: 1 },
    phases: { $value: ["PHASE"] },
    pump_ms: { $value: 1 },
    stage_parts: { $value: ["STAGE_PART_NAME"] },
    fill_ms: { $value: 1 },
    perf_ms: { $value: 1 },
    effects: { $value: ["EFFECT_NAME"] },
    invalidations: { $value: ["INVALIDATION_REASON"] },
    kind_name: { $value: 1 },
    gpu_timed: { $value: 1 },
    gpu_spans: { $value: ["GPU_SPAN_NAME"] },
    gpu_busy_ms: { $value: 1 },
    gpu_px: { $value: 1 },
    scale: { $value: 1 },
    draw_cnt: { $value: 1 },
    triangle_cnt: { $value: 1 },
    gpu_frame: { $value: 1 },
    light_changed: { $value: 1 },
    eye_cast: { $value: 1 },
    eye_ray_cnt: { $value: 1 },
    eye_beam: { $value: 1 },
    eye_sample: { $value: 1 },
    eye_hole_walk: { $value: 1 },
    eye_ask_cnt: { $value: 1 },
    eye_voxel: { $value: 1 },
    eye_hole: { $value: 1 },
    eye_sky: { $value: 1 },
    eye_box_cnt: { $value: 1 },
    light_cast: { $value: 1 },
    light_ray_cnt: { $value: 1 },
    light_beam: { $value: 1 },
    light_sample: { $value: 1 },
    light_hole_walk: { $value: 1 },
    light_ask_cnt: { $value: 1 },
    light_voxel: { $value: 1 },
    light_hole: { $value: 1 },
    light_sky: { $value: 1 },
    light_box_cnt: { $value: 1 },
    loads: { $value: ["BASE_KIND"] },
    fill_brick_cnt: { $value: 1 },
    upload_cnt: { $value: 1 },
    upload_bytes: { $value: 1 },
    heap_used_bytes: { $value: 1 },
  },
  FRAME_GROUP: {
    $description: "FRAME's lanes in groups, every lane in one (lane.test.ts), in the order a reader asks in turn — where the time went, what was drawn and cast, what landed, and what it holds. The trace prints every lane by its group's order, so a lane the core adds is printed without a word written for it; the panel shows some groups, a few rows each, and the report its own lines. The `rays` group's lanes lie in FRAME in its order, which the window's sums of them (STAT.frames.rays) keep.",
    time: {
      $value: [
        "t",
        "interval_ms",
        "refresh_ms",
        "paced_ms",
        "settled",
        "budget_ms",
        "overran",
      ],
    },
    cpu: {
      $value: [
        "tick_ms",
        "phases",
        "pump_ms",
        "stage_parts",
        "fill_ms",
        "perf_ms",
        "effects",
        "invalidations",
      ],
    },
    frame: { $value: ["kind_name"] },
    gpu: {
      $value: [
        "gpu_timed",
        "gpu_spans",
        "gpu_busy_ms",
        "gpu_px",
        "scale",
        "draw_cnt",
        "triangle_cnt",
        "gpu_frame",
        "light_changed",
      ],
    },
    rays: {
      $value: [
        "eye_cast",
        "eye_ray_cnt",
        "eye_beam",
        "eye_sample",
        "eye_hole_walk",
        "eye_ask_cnt",
        "eye_voxel",
        "eye_hole",
        "eye_sky",
        "eye_box_cnt",
        "light_cast",
        "light_ray_cnt",
        "light_beam",
        "light_sample",
        "light_hole_walk",
        "light_ask_cnt",
        "light_voxel",
        "light_hole",
        "light_sky",
        "light_box_cnt",
      ],
    },
    tiles: { $value: ["loads", "fill_brick_cnt"] },
    device: { $value: ["upload_cnt", "upload_bytes"] },
    heap: { $value: ["heap_used_bytes"] },
  },
  TASK: {
    $description: "One settled task (perf/task.rs TaskRecord). `path` is the bytes of the path it opened, zero past their end, and every other word an f64; `start_ms` is NaN for a task that never ran; `stream`, `outcome` and each of `phase_ids` index STREAM_NAME, OUTCOME_NAME and TASK_PHASE_NAME; a run reports each phase at most once, the first `phase_cnt` of `phase_ids` and `phase_vals` in the order it reported them. `at_file` is the offset of the file name, `at_file_sz` long, of the line a failure was made at, in the string table perf.wit `strtab` hands over, or 0 where the table had no room for the name, whose `at_line` is kept; every site word is 0 where the failure was the host's.",
    $extensions: { xpute: { packed: true } },
    stream: { $value: 1 },
    path: { $value: 3 },
    priority: { $value: 1 },
    enqueue_ms: { $value: 1 },
    start_ms: { $value: 1 },
    end_ms: { $value: 1 },
    outcome: { $value: 1 },
    fail: { $value: 1 },
    detail: { $value: 1 },
    at_file: { $value: 1 },
    at_file_sz: { $value: 1 },
    at_line: { $value: 1 },
    phase_cnt: { $value: 1 },
    phase_ids: { $value: ["TASK_PHASE_NAME"] },
    phase_vals: { $value: ["TASK_PHASE_NAME"] },
  },
  WORST: {
    $description: "One of the worst moving frames since the recording started, by its interval, of which the core keeps the longest few (pxl-core perf/record.rs `WORST_CAP`), which fit one page (LIMIT.PAGE_SZ), and hands them over together, longest first (perf.wit `worst`), and what changed from the frame before it: its uploads, their bytes and the heap's high-water mark, each this frame's less that one's, all 0 where `has_prev` is 0. A still interval is long on purpose and is never among them.",
    $extensions: { xpute: { packed: true } },
    sample: { $value: "FRAME" },
    has_prev: { $value: 1 },
    upload_cnt_delta: { $value: 1 },
    upload_delta_bytes: { $value: 1 },
    heap_used_delta_bytes: { $value: 1 },
  },
  PERCENTILE: {
    $description: "A value's percentiles over n values: p50 and p95 each the nearest rank, the least value at or above which lie no more than that share of the n (sorted, the value at ceil(q × n) − 1), and the most.",
    $extensions: { xpute: { packed: true } },
    p50: { $value: 1 },
    p95: { $value: 1 },
    max: { $value: 1 },
  },
  STREAM_STAT: {
    $description: "One stream's tasks in the window, at STAT.tasks.slots + its index × WORDS. Each reason is (fail, detail, n), commonest first; `phase_mean` is NaN for a phase no task reported.",
    $extensions: { xpute: { packed: true } },
    cnt: { $value: 1 },
    ok: { $value: 1 },
    aborted: { $value: 1 },
    err: { $value: 1 },
    lat_p50: { $value: 1 },
    lat_p95: { $value: 1 },
    reason_cnt: { $value: 1 },
    reasons: { $value: ["LIMIT.REASON_CAP", "LIMIT.REASON_WORDS"] },
    phase_n: { $value: 1 },
    phase_mean: { $value: ["TASK_PHASE_NAME"] },
  },
  STEP_STAT: {
    $description: "One registered step's timing, at STAT.steps.slots + its index × WORDS. `name` indexes STEP_NAME, whose phase is STEP_PHASE's (spec/client/core/perf/step.json5).",
    $extensions: { xpute: { packed: true } },
    name: { $value: 1 },
    ms: { $value: 1 },
    cnt: { $value: 1 },
    max_ms: { $value: 1 },
  },
  STAT: {
    $description: "The window's statistics `perf.stats` computes, over its `window_ms`: each section's words at its AT, the fields relative to it. Every word an f64. Packed: a section's AT is where the one before it ends, and WORDS where the last ends, both laid out by the generator.",
    $extensions: { xpute: { packed: true } },
    frames: {
      present: { $value: 1 },
      cnt: { $value: 1 },
      seconds: { $value: 1 },
      moving: { $value: 1 },
      moving_ms: { $value: 1 },
      overran: { $value: 1 },
      gpu_timed: { $value: 1 },
      interval: { $value: "PERCENTILE" },
      tick: { $value: "PERCENTILE" },
      effect: { $value: "PERCENTILE" },
      pump: { $value: "PERCENTILE" },
      stage: { $value: "PERCENTILE" },
      stage_parts_p95: { $value: ["STAGE_PART_NAME"] },
      fill: { $value: "PERCENTILE" },
      fill_brick_cnt: { $value: 1 },
      perf: { $value: "PERCENTILE" },
      effects_p95: { $value: ["EFFECT_NAME"] },
      invalidations: { $value: ["INVALIDATION_REASON"] },
      gpu_busy: { $value: "PERCENTILE" },
      gpu_busy_kinds: { $value: ["FRAME_KIND", 3] },
      phases_p95: { $value: ["PHASE"] },
      gpu_spans_p95: { $value: ["GPU_SPAN_NAME"] },
      gpu_spans_cnt: { $value: ["GPU_SPAN_NAME"] },
      kinds: { $value: ["FRAME_KIND"] },
      gpu_px: { $value: 1 },
      rays: { $value: ["FRAME_GROUP.rays"] },
      heap_used_delta_bytes: { $value: 1 },
      last: { $value: "FRAME" },
    },
    tasks: { slots: { $value: ["STREAM_NAME", "STREAM_STAT"] } },
    steps: {
      cnt: { $value: 1 },
      slots: { $value: ["STEP_NAME", "STEP_STAT"] },
    },
    recording: {
      $description: "What the frames held at the most or the least since the recording started, as the steps are timed, folded as each frame's record is taken (perf/record.rs `perf_fold_recording`): `frame_cnt` the frames folded; the heap's figures by their allocator's names (pxl-core sys/heap.rs `HeapStat`), the most of each but `largest_free`, the least, and `refusals` as it last stood; the body slots' peak (sys/io/body.rs `take_peak`); and `refusals` the tiles each base layer's tile cache refused a slot, summed, in BASE_KIND's order (domain/layer/tile_cache.rs `take_refusal_cnt`). Every word 0 before a frame is folded.",
      frame_cnt: { $value: 1 },
      heap_live_max_bytes: { $value: 1 },
      heap_run_max_bytes: { $value: 1 },
      heap_slot_max_bytes: { $value: 1 },
      heap_range_max_bytes: { $value: 1 },
      heap_largest_free_min_bytes: { $value: 1 },
      heap_refusal_cnt: { $value: 1 },
      body_slots_peak: { $value: 1 },
      refusals: { $value: ["BASE_KIND"] },
    },
  },
  NOW: {
    $description: "What `perf.stats` finds as it reads, the window aside: each section's words at its AT, as STAT lays out its own. Every word an f64.",
    $extensions: { xpute: { packed: true } },
    recording_state: {
      $description: "Whether it records, how long the recording has run, whether it lost what it had no room for (a table's oldest records, or a failure's file name the string table could not hold), and how many frames and tasks its tables hold.",
      recording: { $value: 1 },
      elapsed_ms: { $value: 1 },
      truncated: { $value: 1 },
      frame_cnt: { $value: 1 },
      task_cnt: { $value: 1 },
    },
    draw: {
      $description: "Whether the core draws, as the read finds it, recording or not, every count since the core booted: `frame_cnt` the frames the renderer encoded (pxl-render renderer.rs `drawn_frame_cnt`); `refused_admit` and `refused_stream` the frames that did not run, as the GPU admitted none (pxl-gpu-guest `admit::frame`) or the host still held the stream (pxl-gpu-guest stream.rs) (frame.rs `frame_task`).\nThen the device, as the host wrote its block (spec/gpu/api.json5 DEVICE), the same on the web and natively: `generation` the devices lost so far (pxl-render gpu/api.rs `device_generation`); `status` its STATUS, 0 before the block is written; `err_cnt` the uncaptured errors it raised; and `unfinished` the frames whose work its queue has not done, each a frame the host asked the queue to say done and has not heard of.",
      frame_cnt: { $value: 1 },
      refused_admit: { $value: 1 },
      refused_stream: { $value: 1 },
      generation: { $value: 1 },
      status: { $value: 1 },
      err_cnt: { $value: 1 },
      unfinished: { $value: 1 },
    },
    view: {
      $description: "Where the camera, its pivot and the pointer are as the read finds them, recording or not: `eye_x`..`eye_z`, `dist`, `pivot_x`..`pivot_z`, `hover_x`..`hover_z` and `place_x`..`place_z` in units, angles in radians, `pivot_lon` and `pivot_lat` in degrees and `pivot_ele` in meters, a zoom as its number, and NaN where there is none.\nThe eye is where the camera looks from and the pivot the point it turns about, under the eye in the first-person camera, where the character stands (pxl-core domain/control/camera/controller.rs `pose`, `pivot`).\nThe hover is what the pointer meets, exactly, at the zooms the eye's rays ask, whatever the tool could strike, and `cell_zoom` the zoom the eye's rays draw there (pxl-core domain/query/support.rs `cell_zoom_read`).\nThe pick is what the tool held strikes there (pxl-core domain/control/edit/pick.rs `pick_at`): `hit_kind` what it met, an index into HIT_KIND; `pick_zoom` the zoom of the box struck and `ray_zoom` the rays' there, `folded` 1 where they draw coarser than the box, which strikes nothing. `place_x`..`place_z` is the corner the tool takes (pxl-core domain/control/edit.rs `Hover`), `place_zoom` the zoom it places at, and `blocked` 1 where that room is taken (domain/control/edit/collision.rs `is_placement_blocked`).",
      eye_x: { $value: 1 },
      eye_y: { $value: 1 },
      eye_z: { $value: 1 },
      dist: { $value: 1 },
      polar: { $value: 1 },
      azimuth: { $value: 1 },
      pivot_x: { $value: 1 },
      pivot_y: { $value: 1 },
      pivot_z: { $value: 1 },
      pivot_lon: { $value: 1 },
      pivot_lat: { $value: 1 },
      pivot_ele: { $value: 1 },
      hover_x: { $value: 1 },
      hover_y: { $value: 1 },
      hover_z: { $value: 1 },
      cell_zoom: { $value: 1 },
      hit_kind: { $value: 1 },
      pick_zoom: { $value: 1 },
      ray_zoom: { $value: 1 },
      folded: { $value: 1 },
      place_x: { $value: 1 },
      place_y: { $value: 1 },
      place_z: { $value: 1 },
      place_zoom: { $value: 1 },
      blocked: { $value: 1 },
    },
  },
  TABLE_NAMES: {
    $value: ["frames", "tasks"],
    $description: "The tables the profiler keeps, each read by sequence (perf.wit `table`): the frames and the tasks, oldest first. A task's row never changes once it has landed; a frame's is written again a frame or two later, as its GPU read and its ray counts land (FRAME).",
  },
}
